<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculating theoretical probability for random matatu seat assignments</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A matatu heading to Kisumu has exactly <b>{@total_seats@} empty seats</b> remaining. Upon inspection, <b>{@num_window@} are window seats</b> and <b>{@num_aisle@} are aisle seats</b>.</p>

<p>A group of <b>{@board_pass@} friends</b> board the matatu and are assigned to the empty seats completely at random.</p>

<p><b>a) </b> Calculate the total number of ways the {@board_pass@} friends can be assigned to the available empty seats.</p>
<p>\(n(S) =\) [[input:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>b) </b> Calculate the number of possible seating assignments where <i>exactly</i> <b>{@req_window@} friend(s)</b> get window seats (and the rest get aisle seats).</p>
<p>\(n(E) =\) [[input:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>

<p><b>c) </b> Using your results from parts (a) and (b), determine the theoretical probability that exactly {@req_window@} friend(s) get window seats.</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as a fraction).</i></p>
<p>\(P(\text{exact arrangement}) =\) [[input:ans3]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part a: The Sample Space</b><br>
There are \({@total_seats@}\) empty seats available in total, and \({@board_pass@}\) friends to fill them. The total number of possible random seat assignments is:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle n(S) = {}^{{@total_seats@}}C_{{@board_pass@}} = \frac{{@total_seats@}!}{{@board_pass@}!({@total_seats@} - {@board_pass@})!} = {@ta1@} \)</p>

<p><b>Part b: The Favourable Outcomes</b><br>
The event requires choosing exactly \({@req_window@}\) window seat(s) from the \({@num_window@}\) available, AND the remaining \({@req_aisle@}\) seat(s) from the \({@num_aisle@}\) available aisle seats. We multiply these independent combinations:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle n(E) = {}^{{@num_window@}}C_{{@req_window@}} \times {}^{{@num_aisle@}}C_{{@req_aisle@}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle n(E) = {@window_comb@} \times {@aisle_comb@} = {@ta2@} \)</p>

<p><b>Part c: The Theoretical Probability</b><br>
Theoretical probability is defined as the number of favourable outcomes divided by the total number of equally-likely outcomes in the sample space:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(E) = \frac{n(E)}{n(S)} = \frac{{@ta2@}}{{@ta1@}} \)</p>
<p>Simplifying this fraction mathematically gives the final probability:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ {@ta3@} } \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
